# Goal — report the outcome of the move just executed, then get the next move.
# (On the first call nothing has executed yet: success defaults true.)
bool success        # did the move just executed (follow + spin) succeed? (ignored on the first call)
string mission_path # optional: load this mission YAML before advancing; empty keeps the current one
bool first          # true on the FIRST advance of a fresh tree run -> wipe any prior narrative and reseed. The MissionAdvance BT leaf latches this per run (fresh leaf instance per ExecuteTree goal); an explicit signal, NOT inferred from an empty observation (a mid-run move can legitimately report nothing)
---
# Result — the next move to execute (a grounded trajectory), or the mission's end.
# One cycle of this node now performs BOTH cognition calls: it recompiles the
# narrative (director, via visual_reasoner) AND plans the path (executor, via
# path_planner) over the same frame buffer it owns, and returns the ready-to-drive
# trajectory. mission_done => no trajectory (markers empty, turn 0).
bool mission_done    # true when the mission is over (complete OR failed)
bool mission_failed  # true when it ended in failure (stuck past the cycle cap, or a cognition call failed past its retry budget); false on clean completion
string area          # the current environment (from the narrative)
string message       # on a move: the planner's brief path reasoning; on mission_done: the closing summary or failure reason
# The grounded ground path in normalized image space: point.x, point.y in [-1, 1]
# (center = 0; left/top = -1, right/bottom = +1); z unused. markers[0] is the first
# (nearest) waypoint, markers[-1] the farthest. May be empty for a turn-only move.
geometry_msgs/Point[] markers
# Signed in-place rotation to apply after following the path (degrees), measured from
# the heading the robot ends the path with. + = left (CCW), - = right (CW), 0 = none.
# Executed by the Nav2 Spin behavior.
float64 turn_degrees
# Stamp of the current-view frame the path was planned on (the frame buffer's last
# image). FollowVisualPath grounds the markers into odom using the pose at this stamp.
builtin_interfaces/Time stamp
---
# Feedback
string state         # "RUNNING" while judging / (re)planning
